# Tests for the `lexer` module.

scanWordTest is test
scanWordTest purpose "A word stops at the first space, so `abc def` from offset 0 gives a word of length 3"
scanWordTest verifies scanWord wordIsMaximal
scanWordTest typeParam none
scanWordTest input none
scanWordTest output none
scanWordTest outputOwner none
scanWordTest raises none
scanWordTest effect none
scanWordTest uses none
scanWordTest memory heap false
scanWordTest async false
scanWordTest maxRecursion none
scanWordTest label begin loopKind none
scanWordTest label begin within none
scanWordTest let source immutable String "abc def"
scanWordTest let zero immutable Int64 0
scanWordTest let three immutable Int64 3
scanWordTest at begin do scanFirst
scanWordTest at begin do readLength
scanWordTest at begin do expectThree
scanWordTest at begin return ok none

scanFirst is call
scanFirst in scanWordTest
scanFirst invokes scanWord
scanFirst arg source String source lend
scanFirst arg start Int64 zero copy
scanFirst out firstToken Token
scanFirst ownedBy none
scanFirst cleanedBy none
scanFirst borrows none
scanFirst catch none

readLength is call
readLength in scanWordTest
readLength invokes Token.length
readLength arg record Token firstToken copy
readLength out firstLength Int64
readLength ownedBy none
readLength cleanedBy none
readLength borrows none
readLength catch none

expectThree is call
expectThree in scanWordTest
expectThree invokes test.assertEqualInt64
expectThree arg expected Int64 three copy
expectThree arg actual Int64 firstLength copy
expectThree out none
expectThree ownedBy none
expectThree cleanedBy none
expectThree borrows none
expectThree catch none

classifyWordTest is test
classifyWordTest purpose "The word `is` is classified as the keyword `is`, not as a plain word"
classifyWordTest verifies classifyWord keywordsWin
classifyWordTest typeParam none
classifyWordTest input none
classifyWordTest output none
classifyWordTest outputOwner none
classifyWordTest raises none
classifyWordTest effect none
classifyWordTest uses none
classifyWordTest memory heap false
classifyWordTest async false
classifyWordTest maxRecursion none
classifyWordTest label begin loopKind none
classifyWordTest label begin within none
classifyWordTest let isText immutable String "is"
classifyWordTest let keywordIsKind immutable TokenKind TokenKind.keywordIs
classifyWordTest at begin do classifyIs
classifyWordTest at begin do sameKind
classifyWordTest at begin do expectSame
classifyWordTest at begin return ok none

classifyIs is call
classifyIs in classifyWordTest
classifyIs invokes classifyWord
classifyIs arg word String isText lend
classifyIs out isKind TokenKind
classifyIs ownedBy none
classifyIs cleanedBy none
classifyIs borrows none
classifyIs catch none

sameKind is call
sameKind in classifyWordTest
sameKind invokes TokenKind.equals
sameKind arg left TokenKind isKind copy
sameKind arg right TokenKind keywordIsKind copy
sameKind out kindsMatch Bool
sameKind ownedBy none
sameKind cleanedBy none
sameKind borrows none
sameKind catch none

expectSame is call
expectSame in classifyWordTest
expectSame invokes test.assertTrue
expectSame arg value Bool kindsMatch copy
expectSame out none
expectSame ownedBy none
expectSame cleanedBy none
expectSame borrows none
expectSame catch none
